notes: Founder on device: "Am Ende des Videos bleibt der Sound hängen" (sound hangs at the end) + "soll stabiler werden alles". Root: stopEverything() stopped the transport and camera and RELIED on the PatternEngine.onStop callback to flush held notes — a single point of failure (a held melody/sub note could keep ringing if that callback path was ever out of sync). FIX: stopEverything() now force-silences EVERY voice explicitly and idempotently — pianoRoll.allNotesOff() (clears active-note tracking + releases poly/sub/MIDI/AUv3), panicAllNotesOff() (direct belt-and-suspenders release of synth/subBass/auHost/midiOut), and clears synth.bioModulationEnabled. A "stopEverything: transport + all voices released" breadcrumb confirms it fired on the next device log. ALSO this build (cumulative): rPPG LOCK now CONFIRMED WORKING on the founder's device — the autocorrelation-seed fix produced bpm=81 conf=0.93 (pk=0/low-pk windows now lock via the autocorrelation path); plus rPPG live coaching hints, amp/pk/acf telemetry, the O(1) finger-count + vDSP hot-loop opts, and the dead-code removal. 1 code file for the fix. Compile gate validates; behaviour device-verified on next run.
